  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sandesh begins with making "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "chhena",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chhena"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " from scratch by curdling milk. The result is formed into pieces of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sandesh term",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sandesh-term"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sweetened with sugar and cardamom. Traditional recipes use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "nolen gur",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "nolen-gur"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " when available, but caster sugar is used here for simplicity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not over-knead or over-cook the chhena. The texture should be smooth and slightly moist, not dry and crumbly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "whole-milk",
              "amount": 1500,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lemon",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "juice only",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 80,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "cardamom-green",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "pods",
              "prepNote": "seeds ground to powder",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "pistachios",
              "amount": 20,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "finely chopped, to decorate",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ],
          "defaultServings": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring milk to a full boil in a large saucepan. Stir to prevent burning."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add lemon juice gradually, stirring gently. The milk will curdle within 1-2 minutes. When the whey is clear and yellow, stop adding lemon."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Line a colander with muslin. Pour the curdled milk through. Rinse curds with cold water to remove the sour lemon flavour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tie the muslin and hang it for 30 minutes to drain. Do not press heavily. The chhena should be moist, not dry."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer chhena to a heavy non-stick pan. Add sugar. Cook on low heat, stirring constantly, for 10-12 minutes until the mixture thickens and pulls away from the sides."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from heat. Add ground cardamom. Knead briefly until smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Shape into small rounds or discs. Press a pistachio piece into each. Chill for 1 hour before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Chhena is very dry and grainy after draining",
              "cause": "Over-drained or too much lemon juice added",
              "fix": "Stop draining earlier. Chhena for sandesh should feel like soft plasticine, not crumbly."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Sandesh does not hold its shape and crumbles",
              "cause": "Mixture not cooked long enough in the pan",
              "fix": "Cook until the mixture leaves the sides of the pan cleanly and forms a soft ball. Undercooking leaves too much moisture."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sandesh is the sweet most closely identified with Kolkata. Every neighbourhood has a mishti dokan (sweet shop) with dozens of varieties on display, shaped in wooden moulds carved with flowers, fish, and geometric patterns. The seasonal nolen gur sandesh made in winter from date palm sap is considered the finest version. Sandesh is given as a gift at Durga Puja and other festivals and is eaten at the end of meals."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}